---
import LegalPage from '@/components/info/LegalPage.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/config/site';
import { SMARTKNOB } from '@/data/story';
import { url } from '@/lib/url';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Terms"
  heading="Terms."
  description="Detent's terms in plain words: this is a concept site, nothing is for sale, prices and dates are illustrative, and third-party names belong to their owners."
  summary="Detent One is a concept. Nothing here is for sale, no order you place is real, and no money moves. Enjoy the site, quote it fairly, and please don’t present it as a real store."
  other={{ label: 'Privacy', href: '/legal/privacy/' }}
  dial={{ text: 'TERMS', finish: 'raw', profile: 'wall' }}
>
  <h2>What this site is</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.conceptNotice} The shop, the cart, the reservation and the checkout are working demos. They never take payment and never create an order.
  </p>

  <h2>Prices, dates and specs</h2>
  <p>
    Prices, launch dates, batches, warranty and trial terms describe how the product would be sold. They are design material, not an offer, and they
    create no contract. Specs are design targets.
  </p>

  <h2>People on this site</h2>
  <p>
    The founders, early testers and every quote attributed to them are fictional. Any resemblance to real people is a coincidence. The only real
    person named here is {SMARTKNOB.author}, credited on the <a href={url('/story/')}>story page</a> for the open-source <a href={SMARTKNOB.url} rel="noopener">{SMARTKNOB.name}</a> project that inspired Detent. He has no
    involvement with this site.
  </p>

  <h2>Other companies’ names</h2>
  <p>
    Apps named in the <a href={url('/integrations/')}>integrations directory</a> and elsewhere belong to their owners. They are named only to show what
    the dial would do in them. No company listed has partnered with, endorsed or reviewed Detent. No logos of other companies are used.
  </p>

  <h2>Using what you find here</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Browse, play with the dial, screenshot and screen-record it. That is what it is for.</li>
    <li>Quote the site for commentary, reviews, teaching and design critique, and link back.</li>
    <li>Do not use it, or a copy of it, to take orders, collect payments or pass it off as a real store.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>No warranty on the website</h2>
  <p>
    The site is provided as it is. We work to keep it accurate, fast and accessible, but we do not promise it is free of mistakes, and we are not
    liable for anything that happens because you relied on a concept.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If these terms change, the date at the top changes with them. Questions go to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>, a placeholder address that does not receive mail.</p>
</LegalPage>
